From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:55:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: videobuf2: make the vmalloc allocator selectable

VIDEOBUF2_VMALLOC is normally a hidden dependency selected by in-tree
drivers.  The H713 HDMI diagnostic bridge is intentionally kept out of tree,
so it cannot select the allocator and a defconfig assignment is discarded by
Kconfig.

Give the allocator a prompt so the board defconfig can provide its runtime
dependency without enabling an unrelated media driver.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/common/videobuf2/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/Kconfig
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ config VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
 	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
 
 config VIDEOBUF2_VMALLOC
-	tristate
+	tristate "vmalloc video buffer allocator"
 	select VIDEOBUF2_CORE
 	select VIDEOBUF2_MEMOPS
 	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
